        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0478" n="1132" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1132"/>

                <head>No. 540.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 17, 1875</date>.
                        (Received August 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 448.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I communicated to you in my No. 431 copy
                    and translation of a decree of June 29, for the embargo of all property of
                    Carlists.</p>
                <pb facs="0479" n="1133" xml:id="pg1133"/>
                <p>For the reasons stated in that dispatch, namely, that this decree is one, of the
                    measures of more earnest prosecution of Carl is in, and that it is adopted
                    avowedly in imitation of the policy of the United States in like circumstances,
                    it seems to me needful you should possess a copy of the instructions just issued
                    by the ministry of gobernacion for the execution of the decree in question,
                    which is hereto annexed in original and in translation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. CUSHING.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d241-a1.xml" xpointer="d241-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
